  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Why SNS cannot be a Fetcher",
      "items": [
        "SNS is push and fire-and-forget: no retention, no replay, so there is no past hour to re-fetch",
        "A subscribing Fetcher would lose messages on a crash, and the overwrite rule would then delete the first run's rows",
        "Firehose is the managed service for this job; without it, the Receiver is the piece you build"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What the landing zone buys",
      "items": [
        "SQS buffers 14 days and delivers at least once, so a Receiver outage costs nothing",
        "The Receiver writes to landing/ before deleting from the queue: a crash duplicates, never loses",
        "landing/ is append-only and never overwritten — the replayable log SNS does not give you"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Why bronze does not change",
      "items": [
        "This Fetcher reads landing/ instead of an API, windows by publish time, dedupes on MessageId",
        "Same deterministic path, same one-file-per-window overwrite, same provenance columns",
        "Freshness becomes a heartbeat: for an ad hoc topic, an empty window is normal, not stale"
      ]
    }
  ]
